    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0190" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1024"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/7602</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-30T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7095. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 263. Frothingham. Embassy’s 9154, March 21, 4 p.m., your
                    318. Coordination finally approved. Procedure in operation here <pb facs="0191"
                        n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/> already as to Latin America. Publication changes
                    in lists will be simultaneous.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
